     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"With no defences the attack succeeds: phish_workstation, then pivot_internal, auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc, auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. So at least one control is needed. Every exfiltration path needs admin_db, admin_fileserver or admin_backup. Each of these needs a foothold gained only through auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, and all three require stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin comes only from dump_dbadmin_dc or dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which come only from auth_dc and auth_adfs, both requiring NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore blocks every exfiltration path, so the minimum is 1.\"}"
